<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abd al-Aziz ibn Shu'ayb</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abd <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-aziz">al-Aziz</a> ibn Shu'ayb was the last emir of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a>, ruling from about 949. In 960 the Byzantine general Nikephoros Phokas landed on the island and besieged its capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraklion">Chandax</a>, which fell in March 961. The emir was taken captive to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, and Crete returned to Byzantine rule after nearly 140 years.</p></div>
